            "notes": "Now here's where you can really just get creative. Between here and 5th/6th round, you're just adapting to the enemy. You can really choose Electro Cluster or Moon Landing here if you wanted, and sometimes I'll go Electro Cluster if I'm facing really annoying flying enemies and will combine that with Aerial Distressor. It also helps if you're facing a Brig as she won't be able to hit you from it's max length. \n\nIf you have enough money somehow, I'd immediately grab Cybervenom. So far, it seems like this build's strongest Item combo. Other than Zero-G Suit of course. But honestly, there's really no item other than that that's necessary to make it work. It's a very customizable build, as you can feel free to get rid of pretty much any movement abilities EXCEPT for Zero-G Suit and at least one other movement speed buff. Then play around all you want. Just keep in mind this build focuses on speed. The faster you go, the more horrible the experience for the enemy supports.",
